{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/83514-display-of-grandiose-might-question","id":83514,"title":"Display of Grandiose Might Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-03T15:15:30-08:00","id":83514,"title":"Display of Grandiose Might Question","content":"This Contract states specifically that it can be used for a task that doesn't involve combat. I'm curious what kind of loopholes people have come up with regarding the non-combat clause. <br /> <br /> Is it in the spirit of the law or the letter of the law? Let's say my Gristlegrinder uses it to ramp up his speed to run into a battle. Once he's there, he abruptly decides to perform a sonic flying tackle, the damage enhanced from his speed. If the initial use of speed was simply to join the battle sooner, and was used to indirectly enhance an attack, would the Contract apply?<br /> <br /> Obviously, something as blatant as picking up a car and using it to squash someone is in direct violation. But throwing said car into the path of another car, all but ensuring a brutal accident? If that fair game?<br /> <br /> I've got a street fighting Gristlegrinder ready for play, and I want to make sure he's got a few tricks up his sleeve. He's certainly not above ripping up a lamppost to deter a fight, but he's certainly not above encouraging a fight, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1386-thompry","name":"thompry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1386_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T17:00:06-08:00","id":83595,"title":"","content":"I guess it really depends on how you and your GM define &quot;combat.&quot; If combat, for you, only consists of actions that directly affect a target's Health then I would say that your examples are definitely sneaky little loopholes. Personally, I consider &quot;combat&quot; to be any situation of physical conflict between mutually aware parties; A use of the Athletics skill to sprint to a target with an intent to perform a &quot;sonic flying tackle&quot; is just as much of a &quot;combat roll&quot; as the use of the Brawl skill. Since the Contract cannot boost combat prowess, I do not think that it would allow for Hulk like fights of environmental mayhem. This, however, is just my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T18:30:54-08:00","id":83653,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping that I may be able to sell a lot of the &quot;oops!&quot; moments due to his Intelligence 1. The lad has taken a few too many to the head and ain't as bright as he used to be. On the other hand,his Derangement is Bloodlust, so maybe not. I reckon half the fun will be finding the loopholes as they present themselves. He's a bit of a braggart, so tossing around a Smartcar or two is right up his alley.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1386-thompry","name":"thompry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1386_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T22:21:15-08:00","id":83777,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I guess it all really comes down to intent and whether or not the character is aware of the situation unfolding around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T08:15:35-08:00","id":83962,"title":"","content":"I think my favorite loopholes with this contract were:<br /> <br /> 1) Using the 1-for-1 strength boost + display of grandiose might to get a crazy high strength, then spend a glamour to change it all to manipulation with my dual kithed stonebones/ troll. (surprised the hell out of some people out of combat.)<br /> <br /> 2) less effective all of the time was using it to activate the first clause of the contract. with high enough wyrd you almost keep the str bonus. and if your lucky, get 8 agains","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1445-elesho","name":"elesho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}